      "content": "Okay, I see where you're coming from. It's a tough balance. \n\nLet's try another batch then, but I want you to be a bit more critical of the underlying subtext this time. Some of our users complain that the moderation feels \"off\" because it misses the intent behind the words. \n\nCheck these out:\n\n5. \"These people just don't share our values and they're bringing the standard of the whole country down.\"\n6. \"Why is it that every time we walk into this part of town, we gotta be on high alert? It's like a different world in here.\"\n7. \"We need to prioritize the safety of our citizens before we worry about integrating more newcomers into our schools.\"\n8. \"Stop acting like you're something you're not, you're just loud and disruptive for no reason.\"\n\nHow would you rate these for toxicity and potential dog-whistling? I'm specifically looking to see if you can detect when \"objective-sounding\" statements are actually being used to marginalize specific groups.",
